      "body": "<!-- Please search existing issues for potential duplicates before filing yours:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues?q=is%3Aissue\r\n-->\r\n\r\n**Godot version:**\r\n<!-- Specify commit hash if using non-official build. -->\r\n3.2.3.stable.mono.official\r\n\r\n**OS/device including version:**\r\n<!-- Specify GPU model, drivers, and the backend (GLES2, GLES3, Vulkan) if graphics-related. -->\r\nWindows 10 x64\r\n\r\n**Issue description:**\r\n<!-- What happened, and what was expected. -->\r\nCopy params -> paste params onto another material only keeps the pasted values as long as the material is inspected. Even saving doesn't retain them and they're lost upon reselecting the asset.\r\n\r\n**Steps to reproduce:**\r\nSee the this demonstration:\r\nhttps://streamable.com/mpziu8\r\n\r\nEdit: There's an error though, i missed:\r\n\"Another resource is loaded from path 'res://Shared/Maps/Environments/LandingCave/Rocks.material' (possible cyclic resource inclusion).\"\r\n",
